  "notes": "verify-B4 rerun 2026-10-25 on umbriel-b200-018, harness 0.8 (card: 0.4), source exp/topk-swarm/B4 commit c002a0d9a0, control B1_n6b (approaches/B1 from the same tree), all 24 cells x 2 regimes of the card (N 1024, 4096 x k 16, 64, 256, both requirements), batch state/results/verify-B4/N9_w2fin_vs_B1_n6b_focus_vb4_n9a_20261025_171344.json, named control in one lock section, canaries 32.00098 and 3780 to 3782 us, oracle 22 battery cases passed per cell for variant and control (card: 13), including tie_heavy and pivot_tie where the pivot bin exceeds 32 and the N6 passes run. Code read: the warp finish runs only when the first pass leaves at most 32 items in the pivot bin and did not finish the selection, the items above the bin are scattered by ticket, the bin's members are resolved on warp 0 by redux rounds on (twiddled key, inverted index), exact under both requirements (-0.0 normalized in the prologue under prefer_smaller_index). VERDICT verified = true. Ratios within 3 percent of the card on 40 of 48 cells, the card's conclusions hold: the kill criterion is not met (w2fin is 4.3 to 4.5 percent slower than B1_n6b at bf16 N 1024 and 4096 k 16 not_guaranteed, 1777 against 1701 and 2693 against 2581, card 4.8 and 7.6 percent slower), and the constant-address tickets cost against N9_w2fin2 (same node, consecutive lock sections, B1_n6b within 1.5 percent between the two batches): 52 cycles at bf16 N 1024 k 16, 287 at k 64, 412 at k 256, 123 at N 4096 k 16, 680 at k 64, 1189 at k 256, 1017 at fp32 N 4096 k 256 (card 48 to 1070), the same-kernel A/B of T57 reproduces. Deviations: bf16 N 4096 latency is 2.5 to 8.9 percent lower than the card for the variant and 1.7 to 6.1 percent lower for the control (harness-version effect on striped loads at IPT 16, see card B4_v4_b200_20261025_2), which moves the prefer_smaller_index ratios at N 4096 up by 4.0 to 6.5 percent (1.14x, 1.46x, 1.36x against the card's 1.10x, 1.41x, 1.28x) while the not_guaranteed ratios stay within 3.1 percent. the B1_n6b control at N 1024 k 64 and 256 not_guaranteed is 4.1 to 4.6 percent above the card (2136 and 2430 against 2042 and 2333, both N9 batches agree) while its k 16 cells match within 0.7 percent, cause not isolated (node or the 0.6 chain rotation on a kernel whose second pass runs on a data-dependent share of the inputs), in N9's favor by up to 3 percent on the ratio. bf16 N 1024 k 16 prefer_smaller_index 1.09x against the card's 1.12x. Throughput within 0.2 percent everywhere. Chain fits r2 >= 0.989 (the lowest at bf16 N 4096 k 16 noop). Resources: registers 46 and 40 (latency and throughput kernels) at bf16 N 1024 as the card, 80 and 128 at N 4096, zero spill, SASS instruction counts within 8 of the card's. The B1_n6b control's 4 to 5 percent at N 1024 k 64 and 256 has the same root cause, confirmed by eval-engineer on 2026-10-25 (harness README section 3.1): under the 0.6 rotation the min over repetitions picked the cheaper half of the inputs at chain 8 for a kernel whose pass count depends on the input, fixed in harness 0.10 by fixed strided input subsets per chain length. It is a harness effect, not a node effect."
